  "raw_text": "The session opened with a friction_state around filesystem format: two USB drives formatted NTFS were candidates for the Linux backup target, but NTFS silently drops execute bits, symlinks, and ownership \u2014 exactly the tribal_knowledge a shell-first practitioner holds about what makes a ~/repos directory recoverable versus merely present. The act was assertive \u2014 a claim that NTFS compatibility has no practical value on a machine that will never be handed to Windows \u2014 and it carried sovereign authority because the consequence is irreversible: a backup that cannot restore a working system is not a backup. The resolution came as a declaration: reformat as ext4, preserve WSL as the Windows bridge, close the format question permanently. Harmony was restored not by compromise but by elimination of the false constraint.",
